$ engramdb --no-maintenance --dir [PROJECT] --format plain projects repair --force --no-index
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
This will:
  - re-key the registry entry (subscriptions and worktree links preserved)
  - copy 1 personal memory file(s) and LEAVE the old data directory ([DATA]/projects/[PROJECT_ID]) in place
Re-keyed [PROJECT] from [PROJECT_ID] to [PROJECT_ID].
Copied 1 personal memory(ies) to the live data directory.
  Hint: Memories stay missing from queries until you run `engramdb reindex`.
  The old data directory is left in place ([DATA]/projects/[PROJECT_ID]). It may be shared with another clone of the same remote, so nothing here deletes it — and `engramdb projects prune` will leave it alone too for as long as it holds personal memories, archived transcripts or conversation summaries.
